<span class="cs-line cmt"># Why speculative decoding data is different</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Token acceptance probability (Leviathan et al.)</span>
<span class="cs-line"> </span>
<span class="cs-line hl-p"><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">acceptance_prob</span>(p_target, p_draft, token):</span>
<span class="cs-line">    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">min</span>(<span class="num">1.0</span>, p_target[token] / p_draft[token])</span>
<span class="cs-line"> </span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Expected accepted tokens per step</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># alpha = avg per-token acceptance rate</span>
<span class="cs-line hl-c"><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">expected_tau</span>(alpha, gamma):</span>
<span class="cs-line hl-c">    <span class="kw">return</span> (<span class="num">1</span> - alpha ** (gamma + <span class="num">1</span>)) / (<span class="num">1</span> - alpha)</span>
<span class="cs-line"> </span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># alpha is bounded by KL divergence:</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt">#   alpha &lt;= 1 - 0.5 * sqrt(2 * KL(p_target || p_draft))</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Good data -&gt; low KL -&gt; high alpha -&gt; high tau</span>
<span class="cs-line"> </span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># What "aligned data" means in practice:</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt">#   1. Prompts matching deployment domain</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt">#   2. Responses from target model (not humans)</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt">#   3. Same tokenizer and chat template</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt">#   4. Sequence length matching deployment</span>
<span class="cs-line"> </span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Concrete: EAGLE-3 on same architecture</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># ShareGPT+UltraChat:  tau = 2.82 (Math500)</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Perfect-Blend 1.4M:  tau = 3.48 (Math500)</span>
<span class="cs-line cmt"># Same architecture, +23% tau, +1.17x speedup</span>
      </pre>
